Changes: serial generate/update lifecycle, single configured objective with
maximize/minimize support, callable diversity cells, cross-island inspirations,
and externally composed proposal generation, repair, and evaluation.

These are research recipes, not reproductions of unpublished AlphaEvolve internals.
DGMArchive adapts archive selection only; it does not execute evolving agents.

ShinkaEvolve follows Lange, Imajuku, and Cetin, "ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended
and Sample-Efficient Program Evolution" (Sakana AI), sections 3 and Appendix A.
Official framework: https://github.com/SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve
Local adaptation: RSIKit generate/update lifecycle, caller-owned evaluation,
maximize/minimize support, per-island elite/random archives, bounded resampling,
pooled-maximum reward normalization before expm1, and independently composed
model, embedding, novelty, and meta callbacks. No official framework code is imported.
